[LOSSLESS SOURCE MODEL]
The opt-in --source-model=FILE interface exports lossless source units, parsed
syntax, native bindings, values and segment-aware byte ranges in JSON schema 1.
Its asm-edit-v1 profile requires pure-binary mode and refuses unsupported source
forms without changing ordinary assembly. --source-model-diagnostics=FILE writes
a separate non-certified repair model on failure.
.PP
Static queries may use certified models from exits 0, 4 and 5. Parity-preserving
services must require analysis_outcomes.comparison equal: exit 4 can skip the
comparison, and exit 5 means mismatch. See source-model.md and
source-model.schema.json in the installed documentation.

[SEE ALSO]
The complete manual \(em the full assembly language, every analysis and
reverse-engineering output format, and the linker script language \(em
is installed as
.I xorcyst.texinfo
in this package's documentation directory.
.PP
